<BaseLayout
	title="Gearing Up to Level 30 - Liven's Classic Maple Guide"
	description="What to farm (not buy) on the road to 2nd job. Best mob drops for weapons, shields, gloves, and accessories from Lv 1-30, plus the training spots that double as gear farms."
	currentPath="/guides"
	theme="perion"
	decorations={false}
>
	<section class="section-heading">
		<div>
			<span class="eyebrow eyebrow--guide">Orientation</span>
			<h1>Gearing Up to Level 30</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				NPC shops sell fine gear, but the good stuff drops. This is the
				guide to what's worth chasing versus what to just buy - by class,
				by slot, and by which training spots double as gear farms while
				you push toward 2nd job advancement.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="prose">
		<h2 id="the-philosophy">The gearing philosophy</h2>
		<p>
			Between Lv 1 and Lv 30, most players over-spend on gear. They
			buy every new weapon tier at the shop, replace armor every
			10 levels, and hit the 2nd job job change with 40k meso in
			the bank. That's the wrong loop.
		</p>
		<p>
			The right loop: <strong>buy a cheap weapon at each tier from
			the shop</strong>, but <strong>farm your shield, gloves, shoes,
			and accessories from mobs</strong>. Shop-only slots (chest, pants,
			hat) get one shop piece at Lv 10 and one at Lv 20, then you
			save the rest for potions and the 2nd-job weapon (which is
			the single biggest meso sink pre-40, at ~700k-2M depending
			on class).
		</p>
		<p>
			The list below is every equipment drop with a level requirement
			of 30 or below that our datamine has confirmed. We prioritize
			drops with a MeowDB score of 3+ (means multiple players have
			seen and voted them as consistent). Anything score 1-2 gets
			listed as "rare/possible" - don't camp for it.
		</p>

		<h2 id="universal-picks">Universal picks (any class)</h2>
		<p>
			Three drops are worth going out of your way for regardless of
			what class you rolled. They cover slots where shop options are
			either non-existent or strictly worse:
		</p>

		<div class="pick-grid">
			<div class="pick pick--hero">
				<h3><a href={ITEMS["Pan Lid"]}>Pan Lid</a> (shield, Lv 10)</h3>
				<p class="pick__mob">
					Drops from <a href="/mobs/13">Green Mushroom</a> (Lv 15).{" "}
					<strong>MeowDB score 14</strong> - the single most-confirmed
					drop in the pre-30 table.
				</p>
				<p class="pick__why">
					Any-class shield with meaningful defense at a level where
					most players don't own one. The Lv 10 requirement means it
					slots in immediately after your first job advancement. Farm
					at <strong>West Rocky Mountain III</strong> or{" "}
					<strong>Tree Dungeon, Forest Up North IV</strong> - both are
					also excellent Lv 15-22 EXP maps.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pick pick--hero">
				<h3><a href={ITEMS["Work Gloves"]}>Work Gloves</a> (Lv 10, any)</h3>
				<p class="pick__mob">
					Drops from <a href="/mobs/17">Stirge</a> (Lv 20).
					Score 4.
				</p>
				<p class="pick__why">
					Also the guaranteed quest reward from{" "}
					<a href="/quests/andres-request">Andre's Request</a> at Lv
					10 - so most players don't need to farm this. Listed here
					for completeness: if you skipped the Nella quest chain,
					Stirge in the{" "}
					<strong>Dark Cave / Transfer Area</strong> drop these at
					score 4 (very reliable).{" "}
					<strong>+6 Defense + 1 Critical Rate</strong> and 5 upgrade
					slots make this the base for every scrolled glove pipeline
					later.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pick pick--hero">
				<h3><a href={ITEMS["Weighted Earrings"]}>Weighted Earrings</a> (Lv 20, any)</h3>
				<p class="pick__mob">
					Drops from <a href="/mobs/21">Zombie Mushroom</a> (Lv 24, score
					4) and <a href="/mobs/22">Wild Boar</a> (Lv 25, score 2).
				</p>
				<p class="pick__why">
					Earring slot is usually empty until Lv 30+, but Weighted
					Earrings pop at Lv 20 with real stats. Ant Tunnel III
					farms Zombie Mushrooms for both this AND the White Chaos
					Robe (Lv 35 mage overall - keep it for the future). Best
					accessory upgrade of the pre-30 arc.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2 id="training-spots">Training spots that double as gear farms</h2>
		<p>
			Some maps are worth camping specifically because the mob you're
			grinding drops gear you actually want. Sorted by the level bracket
			they cover:
		</p>

		<table class="farm-table">
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th>Level bracket</th>
					<th>Mob & spot</th>
					<th>What drops here</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 10-15</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/9">Orange Mushroom</a> (Lv 8)<br />
						<em>Henesys Hunting Ground / Dangerous Forest</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<a href={ITEMS["Long Sword"]}>Long Sword</a> (warrior, Lv 10, sc4),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Double Axe"]}>Double Axe</a> (Lv 10, sc4),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Spear"]}>Spear</a> (Lv 10, sc4),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["White Gomushin"]}>White Gomushin</a> shoes (Lv 11)
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 15-22</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/13">Green Mushroom</a> (Lv 15)<br />
						<em>West Rocky Mountain III, Tree Dungeon IV</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<strong><a href={ITEMS["Pan Lid"]}>Pan Lid shield</a> (sc14)</strong>,{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Emerald Staff"]}>Emerald Staff</a> (mage, sc3),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Green Woodsman Boots"]}>Green Woodsman Boots</a> (bowman, sc4)
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 15-20</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/14">Bubbling</a> (Lv 15)<br />
						<em>Line 1 Area 1 (Kerning subway)</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<a href={ITEMS["Battle Axe"]}>Battle Axe</a> (warrior Lv 15, sc3),{" "}
						<strong><a href={ITEMS["Fish Spear"]}>Fish Spear</a> (Lv 20, sc9)</strong>,{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Triple-Tipped Zamadar"]}>Triple-Tipped Zamadar</a> (thief Lv 17, sc6)
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 22-28</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/19">Horny Mushroom</a> (Lv 22)<br />
						<em>Ant Tunnel IV, Ant Tunnel III</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<a href={ITEMS["Steel Fingerless Gloves"]}>Steel Fingerless Gloves</a> (warrior Lv 15, sc5),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Iron Dagger"]}>Iron Dagger</a> (thief/warrior Lv 25, sc2),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Mithril Pole Arm"]}>Mithril Pole Arm</a> (warrior Lv 30, sc2)
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 24-30</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/21">Zombie Mushroom</a> (Lv 24)<br />
						<em>Ant Tunnel III, Ant Tunnel II</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<strong><a href={ITEMS["Weighted Earrings"]}>Weighted Earrings</a> (Lv 20, sc4)</strong>,{" "}
						and <a href={ITEMS["White Chaos Robe"]}>White Chaos Robe</a>{" "}
						(mage Lv 35, sc8 - stash for later)
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 25-30</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/22">Wild Boar</a> (Lv 25)<br />
						<em>West Rocky Mountain IV, Perion Dungeon</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<strong><a href={ITEMS["Eagle Crow"]}>Eagle Crow</a> crossbow (bowman Lv 30, sc4)</strong>,{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Ryden"]}>Ryden</a> bow (Lv 30, sc2),{" "}
						<a href={ITEMS["Weighted Earrings"]}>Weighted Earrings</a>
					</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td class="bracket">Lv 28-32</td>
					<td>
						<a href="/mobs/30">Fire Boar</a> (Lv 32)<br />
						<em>The Burnt Land III/IV/V</em>
					</td>
					<td>
						<strong><a href={ITEMS["Fireman's Axe"]}>Fireman's Axe</a> (warrior Lv 30, sc4)</strong>{" "}
						- a top-tier pre-job-change axe. Slight over-level to
						grind solo; go in a party for EXP anyway.
					</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>

		<h2 id="warrior-picks">Warrior gear picks</h2>
		<p>
			Warriors have the deepest weapon-drop pool because they can
			wield swords, axes, blunt weapons, spears, and polearms. The
			winning play here is: buy shop swords for the Lv 1-15 arc
			(too many drops beat them to bother farming), then chase the
			named weapons below for the Lv 15-30 arc.
		</p>

		<ul class="drop-list">
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Battle Axe"]}>Battle Axe</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, warrior-only, score 3) - drops from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/14">Bubbling</a>. Solid axe with a low enough req
				that you'll actually use it for the full Lv 15-25 stretch.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Steel Fingerless Gloves"]}>Steel Fingerless Gloves</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, warrior, score 5) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/19">Horny Mushroom</a> in Ant Tunnel. Best
				score-per-effort in the whole warrior list.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Mithril Pole Arm"]}>Mithril Pole Arm</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, warrior, score 2) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/19">Horny Mushroom</a>. Rare-ish but worth
				camping if you're going Spearman 2nd job.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Fireman's Axe"]}>Fireman's Axe</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, warrior, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/30">Fire Boar</a> in The Burnt Land. This is the
				axe you want going into Fighter/Page 2nd job change.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Black Dragon Robe"]}>Black Dragon Robe</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, warrior, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/36">Lorang</a> at Florina Beach. The chest slot
				pre-30 is usually a "buy from shop" but this beats every shop
				option cleanly.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="callout callout--tip">
			<strong>Skip:</strong>{" "}
			<a href={ITEMS["Wooden Sword"]}>Wooden Sword</a> (Lv 10, sc4) -
			lands too early, gets replaced within a level. Same with{" "}
			<a href={ITEMS["Metal Axe"]}>Metal Axe</a> (Lv 10, warrior-tagged)
			- the <a href={ITEMS["Long Sword"]}>Long Sword</a> from Orange
			Mushroom is a better use of your time.
		</p>

		<h2 id="magician-picks">Magician gear picks</h2>
		<p>
			Magicians live and die by INT-scaling gear, and INT-tagged
			staff drops are surprisingly common in the pre-30 arc. Buy
			the Lv 8 wand from Grendel the Really Old, then farm the
			following:
		</p>

		<ul class="drop-list">
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Emerald Staff"]}>Emerald Staff</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, mage-only, score 3) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/13">Green Mushroom</a>. Same map as Pan Lid, so
				one training spot outfits both your weapon and shield slot.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Wizard Staff"]}>Wizard Staff</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 25, mage-only, score 2) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/16">Blue Mushroom</a> at The Entrance of Golem's
				Temple. Bridges you cleanly from the Emerald Staff to your
				2nd-job elemental wand at Lv 30.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Beige Plain Robe"]}>Beige Plain Robe</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, mage, score 1) - from <a href="/mobs/6">Stump</a>. Score
				is low but Stumps are trivial to farm; grab one if you see it
				drop while doing early Ellinia quests.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Blue Basic Boots"]}>Blue Basic Boots</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10, mage, score 2) - from <a href="/mobs/17">Stirge</a>.
				Same farm as Work Gloves, so kill two birds with one bat.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Lemona"]}>Lemona</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, mage, score 3) - gloves from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/7">Slime</a>. Trivial farm at any Ellinia
				dungeon; drop rate is high.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="bowman-picks">Bowman gear picks</h2>
		<p>
			Bowmen have the smallest drop pool but the most concentrated
			one: Wild Boar carries both viable 2nd-job weapons, which
			means one training spot pre-30 answers your Lv 30 weapon
			question regardless of whether you go Hunter or Crossbowman.
		</p>

		<ul class="drop-list">
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Eagle Crow"]}>Eagle Crow</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30 crossbow, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/22">Wild Boar</a> at West Rocky Mountain IV.
				Score 4 means you'll see 2-3 of these in a solid grinding
				session. Best Crossbowman starter weapon in the game.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Ryden"]}>Ryden</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30 bow, score 2) - from <a href="/mobs/22">Wild Boar</a>{" "}
				and <a href="/mobs/30">Fire Boar</a>. Rarer than Eagle Crow; if
				you're going Hunter, camp the same map anyway - a Fireman's Axe
				or Eagle Crow sells to a Warrior/Crossbowman party mate for
				real meso.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["War Bow"]}>War Bow</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10 bow, score 1) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/10">Ribbon Pig</a>. Marginal, but Ribbon Pig
				farming for the Old Wisconsin quest was going to happen anyway.
				Skip if you already bought the Lv 10 shop bow.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Brown Hard Leather Boots"]}>Brown Hard Leather Boots</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10 bowman, score 1) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/9">Orange Mushroom</a>. Same farm as the Long
				Sword; keep an eye out but don't camp.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Green Woodsman Boots"]}>Green Woodsman Boots</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15 bowman, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/13">Green Mushroom</a>. Best pre-30 bowman shoes.
				Same farm as Pan Lid and Emerald Staff (Green Mushroom is
				genuinely the best gear-and-EXP combo map in the game).
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="thief-picks">Thief gear picks</h2>
		<p>
			Thieves get punished hardest by weapon shop prices (claws and
			daggers scale hard with level requirements), so the drop route saves the
			most meso here. If you're going Assassin (claw) the drop table
			is thin - buy shop claws through Lv 30. If you're going Bandit
			(dagger), the drops below are excellent (weapon req level
			scaling is steep for both weapons):
		</p>

		<ul class="drop-list">
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Triple-Tipped Zamadar"]}>Triple-Tipped Zamadar</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 17 dagger, score 6) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/14">Bubbling</a> at Kerning subway. Score 6 is
				one of the highest in the whole pre-30 table - this drop is
				almost expected in a grinding session.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Iron Dagger"]}>Iron Dagger</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 25 thief/warrior, score 2) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/19">Horny Mushroom</a> and{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/1001">Jr. Sentinel</a>. Ant Tunnel is your best
				dagger-farm map for the Lv 22-28 window.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Stinger"]}>Stinger</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 22 thief, score 1) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/18">Jr. Necki</a>. Rare but drops in the same
				region you're doing Kerning PQ around, so worth noting.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Bronze Wolfskin"]}>Bronze Wolfskin</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 25 thief gloves, score 1) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/32">Jr. Wraith</a>. Rare drop but meaningful
				stat block if you find one.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong><a href={ITEMS["Garnier"]}>Garnier</a></strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10 claw, score 1) - from <a href="/mobs/8">Pig</a>. The ONE
				decent claw drop in the pre-30 pool. Assassins should still
				just buy shop claws unless this shows up incidentally.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="hats">Hats (the slot I told you to skip)</h2>
		<p>
			Full transparency: my first draft of this guide told you to buy
			the Lv 10 shop hat and forget about the slot. Then I re-ran the
			datamine audit and it laughed at me - there are{" "}
			<strong>ten</strong> pre-Lv30 hat drops with score{" "}
			<code>&gt;=3</code> that any class would actually equip, and
			most of them come from mobs already in your farm table. Zero
			new maps required. Here's the corrected picture.
		</p>

		<h3 id="hats-universal">The one hat every class should chase</h3>
		<p class="callout callout--tip">
			<strong>
				<a href={ITEMS["Red Starry Bandana"]}>Red Starry Bandana</a>
			</strong>{" "}
			(Lv 25, all-job, score 8) - drops from{" "}
			<a href="/mobs/17">Stirge</a> in Sleepywood. +2 STR, 24 PDD, 5
			MaxHP. There is no shop hat in the Lv 20-30 range that comes
			within 10 PDD of this. Stirge is already your Work Gloves +
			Blue Basic Boots farm - three drops from one map.
		</p>

		<h3 id="hats-mage">Magician-only hats</h3>
		<p>
			Mages get the deepest hat pool - four class-locked options across
			the Lv 10-30 window:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Red Apprentice Hat"]}>Red Apprentice Hat</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10, score 8) - from <a href="/mobs/14">Bubbling</a>.
				Same map as your Emerald Staff / Battle Axe / Triple-Tipped
				Zamadar farm; Bubbling is genuinely the busiest single map
				in the pre-30 gear routing.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Pink Jester"]}>Pink Jester</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, score 7) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/21">Zombie Mushroom</a>. Requires INT 50 / LUK
				20, so it lands right at the Lv 30 job-change boundary. This
				is your "walk into 2nd job with a real hat" pick.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Black Jester"]}>Black Jester</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, score 6) - from <a href="/mobs/20">Dark Axe Stump</a>{" "}
				in Perion. Slight sidegrade to Pink Jester (+15 MaxMP
				instead of +15 MaxHP). Grab whichever drops first.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Brown Jester"]}>Brown Jester</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 30, score 3) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/19">Horny Mushroom</a>. The +3 INT tradeoff
				loses some MaxHP; a mage who cares more about damage than
				survival should farm this over the other Jesters.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 id="hats-warrior-bowman-thief">Warrior / Bowman / Thief hats</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Bronze Koif"]}>Bronze Koif</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10, Warrior, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/7">Slime</a>. Trivial farm at Ellinia Dungeon
				and it lines up with your Lemona gloves drop.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Green Feather Hat"]}>Green Feather Hat</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, Bowman, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/13">Green Mushroom</a>. The same map that
				gives you Pan Lid + Green Woodsman Boots + Emerald Staff
				now covers your hat slot too. Green Mushroom is
				disgustingly generous.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Red Thief Hood"]}>Red Thief Hood</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 15, Thief, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/12">Octopus</a> in Kerning. Sits alongside
				the Triple-Tipped Zamadar drops - if you're grinding subway
				Bubblings you'll pass Octopus maps anyway.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["Green Loosecap"]}>Green Loosecap</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 20, Thief, score 4) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/16">Blue Mushroom</a> at the Entrance of
				Golem's Temple. Bridges the Red Thief Hood -> job change
				window.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3 id="hats-fallback">Universal fallback (any class)</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>
					<a href={ITEMS["White Bandana"]}>White Bandana</a>
				</strong>{" "}
				(Lv 10, all-job, score 3) - from{" "}
				<a href="/mobs/7">Slime</a>. Score 3 is the "don't camp,
				but grab it if you see it" tier. Fine bridge from Lv 10 to
				15 if the Red Apprentice Hat doesn't drop.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="callout callout--tip">
			<strong>Punch line update:</strong> the "three map plan"
			(Green Mushroom, Ant Tunnel, Wild Boar) now covers your hat
			slot too. Add Stirge to the rotation between Lv 20-25 for the
			Red Starry Bandana and you've got a complete Lv 10-30 kit from
			four maps.
		</p>

		<h2 id="what-not-to-chase">What NOT to chase</h2>
		<p>
			The mob drop table has a lot of noise. Skip these:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Anything with score 0 or negative.</strong> The one-off
				drops that appear in the tables but no one has actually
				confirmed. Not worth camping.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Cosmetic tops/bottoms.</strong> There are 28 tops and
				20 bottoms in the pre-30 drop table with wildly varying stats -
				but Lv 10 shop chest armor + Lv 20 shop pants covers the
				stat block just fine. Cosmetics are for after 2nd job.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Lv 0 "beginner" weapons</strong> (Sword,{" "}
				<a href={ITEMS["Hand Axe"]}>Hand Axe</a>,{" "}
				<a href={ITEMS["Razor"]}>Razor</a>) - these drop before you can
				use them meaningfully. The shop-bought Lv 8 weapon skips over
				the whole tier.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Duplicate low-tier Stumps drops.</strong>{" "}
				<a href={ITEMS["Wooden Wand"]}>Wooden Wand</a>,{" "}
				<a href={ITEMS["Composite Bow"]}>Composite Bow</a>,{" "}
				<a href={ITEMS["Juno"]}>Juno</a> gloves - all mediocre score,
				all replaced within 5 levels. Not worth stopping training for.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 id="the-punch-line">The punch line</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Pick one map, farm it hard.</strong> Green Mushrooms at
			West Rocky Mountain III is the single best training spot in
			the Lv 15-22 window: Pan Lid for shield, Emerald Staff or
			Green Woodsman Boots depending on class, and clean EXP that
			gets you to Kerning PQ. Then move to Ant Tunnel III/IV for the
			Lv 22-28 window (Horny Mushroom + Zombie Mushroom on adjacent
			maps), grab your Weighted Earrings and Steel Fingerless Gloves,
			and finish the Lv 28-30 grind at Wild Boar for Eagle Crow or
			Fireman's Axe.
		</p>
		<p>
			Three maps. Six meaningful drops. About 15 hours of gameplay.
			You'll hit Lv 30 with a full accessory kit, a good weapon,
			and enough banked meso to buy your 2nd-job weapon at the
			job change - which is the outcome most players don't achieve
			because they're broke from over-buying shop gear.
		</p>

		<p class="verification">
			<strong>Data provenance:</strong> mob drop tables from MeowDB
			(<a href="https://meowdb.com/msclassic" target="_blank" rel="noopener">meowdb.com/msclassic</a>),
			item stats + level requirements from the CoT 2 client datamine.
			MeowDB scores are community upvotes minus downvotes (public
